    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68583" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μονομᾰχ-έω</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουνο-</span></b> , fut. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ήσω</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Men.
			<u>Sam.</u>
			225
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μονομάχος</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fight in single combat</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1220
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> with one, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				391e
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					35.5.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοῦνοι Ἑλλήνων μουνομαχήσαντες τῷ
				Πέρσῃ</span>
			<i>having fought singlehanded</i> with the Persians, of the
			Athenians at Marathon, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυοῖσι οὐκ ἂν μουνομαχέοιμι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.104
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>fight as a gladiator</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tox.</u>
				58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				1.17.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				75.16
			</span></i>.</div>
